## Source-First Inventory

This inventory was recorded after one opening of the original PNG and before
reading the author's spec, render, SVG, context, or result.

Source: ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/8a/figures/fig-32.png

SHA-256: f8cb6f416038ce000c219ba8ea97cb40f210f0411cfb5525ee4291730d6f1789

- One shared Cartesian coordinate frame, not separate subfigures or a grid.
- Horizontal x axis and vertical y axis meet at the origin, labeled O below
  and left. Both have positive arrowheads and short negative-direction tails.
- Both axes number 2, 4, and 6. Intermediate unit marks are unnumbered;
  the x scale visibly continues through 7, and the y scale through 6.
- Three labeled filled endpoints: B at (1,2), A at (3,5), C at (6,1).
  These values are read from the original ticks and projections, not an answer.
- Solid BA rises rightward from B to A. Solid BC descends rightward from B
  to C. They meet only at B; there is no AC segment or closed triangle fill.
- Three vertical dashed projections descend from B, A, and C to the x axis
  at x=1, x=3, and x=6, respectively.
- The x=3 projection intersects the interior of BC but has no point marker or
  extra label there. That crossing is not a fourth mathematical point.
- Visible labels are A, B, C, O, x, y and six numeric tick labels; the source
  contains no coordinate-pair annotations, solution construction, or caption
  within this crop.
- Source raster wear and uneven strokes are not mathematical requirements.
  Regularized unit spacing, clean geometry, semantic colors, enlarged text,
  and marker/line styling must be identified separately as modern choices.

