## Inventory Mapping

- O maps to origin-label at [0,0] in the common x-axis/y-axis frame.
  B-source-coordinate, A-source-coordinate, and C-source-coordinate all
  use that same literal origin as their displacement reference.
  O is an axis intersection and label, not a fourth filled point.
  orthogonal-coordinate-frame preserves the shared perpendicular axes.
- B, A, and C map to the same-named point objects and the three exact
  source-coordinate displacement assertions. BA-source-displacement
  covers B/A with [2,3]; BC-source-displacement covers B/C with [5,-1].
  Thus every filled source point is covered by an executable relationship
  wholly inside each applicable pointRelationships inventory group.
  No point is justified only by objectCount or an unrelated point pair.
- The two existing applicable source groups explicitly require
  pointRelationships. The independent combined origin/points inventory
  maps O's literal [0,0] and its label as well as B/A/C; the origin-relative
  displacements are wholly within that combined source frame.
- BA and BC map to solid segment objects and BA-endpoints/BC-endpoints.
  Exactly these two solid branches are present, meeting at B. No AC,
  closing edge, triangle fill, graph extension, or plotted query point
  has been added.
- Three guides map to B-x-projection, A-x-projection, C-x-projection.
  Each has an endpoint assertion to [1,0], [3,0], or [6,0] and a
  perpendicular-to-x-axis assertion. Their rendered dash pattern is 5,5.
  The A guide crosses BC without an extra marker or label.
- Positive arrows map to x-positive-arrow/y-positive-arrow and their
  connects assertions. Both short negative tails remain visible.
- Seven x ticks and six y ticks preserve unit indexing in this shared
  frame; only 2,4,6 are labeled on each axis. These are axis tick lists,
  not a source grid or lattice; gridDimensions is not applicable.
- Twelve visible text labels are exactly 2,4,6 on each axis, B,A,C,O,x,y.
  Three visible source markers are filled. The full current PNG shows
  all labels and geometry within the canvas, with clear separation.

